    "title": "Bradley plays final exhibition game Thursday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kurt Pegler ,\n27 minutes ago\nPEORIA, Ill. (WMBD/WYZZ) — One more dress rehearsal.\nBradley hosts St. Louis in its final exhibition game of the season Thursday. Brian Wardle says he plans on playing a lot of his players to get ready for the season opener Nov. 3.\nThe Braves have nine players on the roster that are listed as freshmen or sophomores.\n“It’s hard for all freshmen, now. Teams are usually (playing older players) but you learn a lot as a freshman,” said Wardle. “You’re going to have good days, bad days, good weeks, bad weeks. You just have to stay the course, stay consistent with your work ethic, your approach and routine. That’s what I think those freshmen are learning. That’s going to really help those guys because they have a lot of talent.”\nSt. Louis is coached by former Indiana State coach Josh Schertz. Game time is 7 p.m. Thursday.\nBradley opens the season a week from Monday against St. Bonaventure.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CIProud.com.",
